{
  "type": "Collection",
  "id": "night-train-services",
  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "Every night-train service in Europe as curated by [Back-on-Track Europe](https://back-on-track.eu/) — 410 services run by 31 operators (39 distinct operator codes — joint services like PKP/ČD carry compound codes), snapshot **2026-08** of the Open Night Train Database (ONTD).\n\nEach feature is one service (one train number, one calendar pattern) with its operator, origin/destination, principal via stations, travel classes, running days and known irregularities. **Geometry is schematic**: straight segments connecting the curated stops in running order — it shows the network's structure, not the physical track alignment. For the designed cartographic view of the same data, see the [Back-on-Track night train map](https://back-on-track.eu/night-train-map/) (also available in print).\n\nThe default style colors services by operator:\n\n| Color | Operator | Services |\n|---|---|---|\n| 🟦 `#2a78d6` | UZ (Ukrainian Railways) | 118 |\n| 🟧 `#eb6834` | ÖBB (Nightjet) | 32 |\n| 🟩 `#1baf7a` | FS (Intercity Notte) | 30 |\n| 🟨 `#eda100` | PKP | 26 |\n| 🩷 `#e87ba4` | CFR | 26 |\n| 💚 `#008300` | SNCF (Intercités de Nuit) | 18 |\n| 🟪 `#4a3aa7` | PKP/ČD | 14 |\n| 🟥 `#e34948` | TCDD | 14 |\n| ⬜ `#898781` | all other operators | 132 |\n\nThe interactive data page renders this collection with a style switcher (operators / seasonal / motorail). Field semantics, join keys and runnable queries are in the [agent guide](AGENTS.md). Attribute tables without geometry live in the sibling collection [night-train-network-attributes](../night-train-network-attributes/collection.json).",
